 ### MCOP GPU Ray-Casting Pipeline
-A GPU-based volume rendering pipeline that uses a Mixed Camera and Object Perspective (MCOP) projection to render light fields for displays with holographic screens, bypassing rasterizer interpolation limitations [S2]. It differs from standard single-pass GPU ray-casters because it cannot rely on rasterizer interpolation to pass combined 3D and projected data from vertex to fragment shader due to MCOP perspective [S2]. The pipeline renders proxy geometry (coarsely tessellated bounding volume) to a fragment shader, where the vertex shader computes MCOP projection and passes normalized/unnormalized projected coordinates to the fragment stage for ray computation and compositing [S2].
