 ### CUDAVolumetricRender
-A hardware-accelerated volumetric rendering function provided by CUDALink for CUDA-capable graphics cards, performing real volume rendering [S4, unofficial]. It requires the latest CUDA paclet and converts slices to a packed integer array with depth 3, elements 0-255. It repartitions data dimensions from $d \times h \times w$ to $h \times w \times d$ without changing data order, then calls `CUDAVolumetricRender` [S4, unofficial]. This is a 'real deal' volumetric renderer with a transfer function, unlike polygon-based methods which mimic the effect [S4, unofficial]. Pitfall: The function requires specific data repartitioning and may throw memory allocation errors [S4, unofficial].
